# bodymd

When the user talks about meals, training, weight, waist, sleep, calories, protein,
eating order, or "my cut" — **read `SKILL.md` at the repo root first.** It is the operator
manual and it defines the data contract that `log/*.md` must follow.

## Hard rules — do not break these

- **`log/*.md` is append-only.** Never rewrite or delete a line.
- Corrections go through `edited: <what changed and why>`, never by editing the original.
- **Every nutrition line needs `source:`** — one of `photo`, `voice`, `manual`, `wearable`,
  `video+voice`, `estimated`.
- **Write `unknown` rather than guessing.** A fabricated number is worse than a gap.
- **Never modify `profile.md`** without explicit confirmation from the user.
- **No medical advice.** Estimates only — no diagnoses, no promised outcomes.

## Where things live

| Path | What it is |
|---|---|
| `SKILL.md` | Operator manual — read this first |
| `workflows/` | Meal log, training log, daily report, weekly review |
| `templates/` | `profile.md`, `daily-log.md`, `report.md` |
| `scripts/` | `validate_log.py`, `parse_log.py`, `selftest.py` |
| `docs/run-with-any-model.md` | Setup for each AI tool |
